5. Failed assertions, in full

- e2e-queue-full/faults.sql (test/analysis/e2e-queue-full/faults.sql) over 3 runs
  claim: e2e-queue-full: more clients than connections plus queue: exactly the three over the bound were shed (53M01).
  1 violating rows:
    e2e-queue-full/2/base: row 2, shed 3

- load-errors/report:loadgen-answered (test/analysis/report/sections/check-loadgen-answered.sql) over 1 runs
  claim: load tool conservation, per instance in the final flush: every sent request has a final outcome or is still in flight (sent = completed over ok, db-error, refused and lost + in_flight).
  1 violating rows:
    load-errors/42/1764201600000000000 loadgen-1: sent 197, completed 198, in_flight 0

- load-errors/report:loadgen-conservation (test/analysis/report/sections/check-loadgen-conservation.sql) over 1 runs
  claim: load tool conservation, per instance in the final flush: every intended request was sent, could not be sent, or is still queued (intended = sent + could_not_send + queued).
  1 violating rows:
    load-errors/42/1764201600000000000 loadgen-1: intended 200, sent 197, could_not_send 2, queued 0

6. Oracle mismatches, in full

- e2e-queue-full/rows.sql (test/analysis/e2e-queue-full/rows.sql) over 3 runs
  claim: e2e-queue-full: every proxy-made error a client saw is counted under its error-contract row, and every counted row for a request reached a client: shed = 53M01, unsupported-feature + unsupported-extended = 0A000, lost-after-read = 08006, lost-after-write = 08007.
  1 violating rows:
    e2e-queue-full/2/base: shed 2, c53m01 3, unsupported 0, c0a000 0, after_read 0, c08006 0, after_write 0, c08007 0

